  "identity": {
    "playing_style": "Red Bull DNA: vertical, transition-heavy football with aggressive counter-pressing and young athletic profiles. Ole Werner (2025/26, sacked June 2026 despite 3rd place and 65 points) rebuilt after losing key players and had no European football to manage. Demichelis, appointed within five days of Werner's exit, brings a more possession-oriented positional game from his River Plate title-winning side; he opened 2026/27 with a 4-3-3 (Vandevoordt; Baku, Orbán, Lukeba, Raum; Banzuzi, Seiwald, Reitz; Nusa, Gomis, Gruda) and a 3-0 win over Gladbach.",
    "principles": [
      "under-24 recruitment with resale value",
      "Red Bull multi-club network (Salzburg, New York, Bragantino)",
      "coach must fit the system, not vice versa",
      "sell one star per summer"
    ],
    "club_character": "Corporate-backed club founded 2009; small but growing fan base; low fan pressure but high boardroom expectations; polarising in German football culture because of the 50+1 workaround.",
